      "text": "\\(19:8\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "e",
    "value": "19:8"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1989-p15.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(AD=m\\) and \\(DC=9-m.\\) Stewart’s Theorem gives \\[ \\begin{gathered} 7^2m+5^2(9-m) \\\\ =9\\bigl(5^2+m(9-m)\\bigr). \\end{gathered} \\] Simplifying yields \\(9m^2-57m=0,\\) so \\(m=\\frac{19}{3}.\\) Then \\(DC=\\frac{8}{3},\\) and \\(AD:DC=19:8.\\)\n\nThus the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Let \\(AD=m\\) and \\(DC=9-m\\)",
        "Apply Stewart’s Theorem to cevian \\(BD\\)"
      ],
